   133	        <p data-layer="narrative">The March 11 G7 presidency communique welcomed a release of "de libérer jusqu’à 400 millions de barils de réserves stratégiques", to release up to 400 million barrels of strategic reserves.<Cite s="elysee-g7-communique-2026-03-11" passage="de libérer jusqu’à 400 millions de barils de réserves stratégiques" /></p>
   134	        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="2">Weekly U.S. retail diesel was {prices.dieselSep28} dollars a gallon on September 28. On March 2 the same series was {prices.dieselMar2}. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said American farmers, truckers, and businesses should not be left carrying the burden of a global diesel shortage.<Cite s="gasdesw-2026-10-03" passage="2026-09-28,6.382" /><Cite s="gasdesw-2026-10-03" passage="2026-03-02,3.897" /><Cite s="bessent-post-2026-10-01" passage="American farmers, truckers, and businesses should not be left carrying the burden of a global diesel shortage" /></p>
   135	        <QuoteCard speaker="Scott Bessent, Treasury secretary" when="October 1, 2026" where="X post" label="Treasury secretary">
   136	          <p>American farmers, truckers, and businesses should not be left carrying the burden of a global diesel shortage.<Cite s="bessent-post-2026-10-01" passage="American farmers, truckers, and businesses should not be left carrying the burden of a global diesel shortage" /></p>
   137	        </QuoteCard>
   138	        <p data-layer="narrative">Germany's emergency FAQ says "Deutschlands Notfallreserve für etwa 90 Tage umfasst insgesamt etwa 20 Millionen Tonnen", a reserve of about 20 million tonnes for about 90 days. Germany's emergency FAQ of October 1, the day before the G7 decision, says a first tranche of the volumes Germany set aside for release has been drawn by market participants, and "Derzeit wird vom Markt keine weitere Freigabe für erforderlich gehalten", the market does not consider a further release necessary at present.<Cite s="bundesregierung-energy-faq-2026-10-01" passage="Deutschlands Notfallreserve für etwa 90 Tage umfasst insgesamt etwa 20 Millionen Tonnen" /><Cite s="bundesregierung-energy-faq-2026-10-01" passage="Eine erste Tranche dieser für die Freigabe vorgesehenen Mengen wurde mittlerweile von den Marktteilnehmern abgerufen" /><Cite s="bundesregierung-energy-faq-2026-10-01" passage="Derzeit wird vom Markt keine weitere Freigabe für erforderlich gehalten." /></p>
   139	        <p data-layer="narrative">U.S. stocks of distillate fuel oil were 105,180 thousand barrels in the week of September 25, against 103,391 thousand in the week of August 21.<Cite s="eia-distillate-2026-10-03" passage="Stocks of Distillate Fuel Oil" /><Cite s="eia-distillate-2026-10-03" passage="(Thousand Barrels)" /><Cite s="eia-distillate-2026-10-03" passage="08/21/26 08/28/26 09/04/26 09/11/26 09/18/26 09/25/26 View History U.S. 103,391 104,187 106,274 107,859 107,431 105,180" /></p>
   140	        <p data-layer="narrative">The European Commission's Energy Union task force said EU diesel supply remains stable for the time being, but prices remain high.<Cite s="ec-taskforce-2026-10-02" passage="EU diesel supply remains stable for the time being, but prices remain high" /></p>
