   153	          <p>On September 29 the Energy Department issued a request for an "exchange of up to 40 million barrels of crude oil" from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve. Secretary Chris Wright said several European member countries "have released only a fraction" of what they pledged. The department said five earlier solicitations "collectively awarded more than 133 million barrels," with a "25 percent premium in returned barrels," and that these exchanges will also ensure the reserve continues to be refilled, while saving taxpayers more than $3 billion. Bids are due "October 6, 2026." The oil is to come from Big Hill and Bryan Mound.<Cite s="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" passage="an exchange of up to 40 million barrels of crude oil" /><Cite s="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" passage="collectively awarded more than 133 million barrels" /><Cite s="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" passage="several European member countries have released only a fraction" /></p>
